No pi source is included in this repository, and none is vendored. This
directory records a LEARN-ONLY decision and the evidence behind it.

pi is MIT, which would pass the §9.11 gate if anything were copied from it.
Nothing is, because §9.11's LOCKED table grades earendil-works/pi NO —
"concepts/behavior/UX only — reimplement through CrossOS contracts" — the
same grade rectangle and Amethyst carry, and the same reason: what CrossOS
needed from it is the SHAPE of a resource registry, not its code.

This directory lives here rather than under third_party/ for the same reason
docs/references/alt-tab-macos does. The merge gate's model is "this directory
holds something we copied or adapted", and a decision not to copy is a
different thing. The two gates would otherwise disagree about what a learn-only
entry is.

The reference clone is at .tmp/research/pi, is not a dependency, is not built,
and is not required to build, test or ship CrossOS.
